# packages/goodies.list — the batteries. Everything here is baked into the
# image: no install-time selection, the distro ships complete (decision
# revised in docs/BLUEPRINT.md §14 — we don't ask, we deliver).
#
# NVIDIA drivers are NOT here: blindly installing them blacklists nouveau
# and breaks non-NVIDIA machines. ii-post-install auto-detects the GPU and
# installs the right variant from the on-ISO stash (packages/nvidia.list).

# CLI quality-of-life stack
# bash-completion loads our /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/iictl on the
# installed system (fish/zsh load their vendor completions natively).
bash-completion
# Shell layer (#15) — the baked bits the `iictl shell` chooser needs. fish +
# starship already arrive as upstream PKGBUILD deps (illogical-impulse-fonts-
# themes), so they are NOT re-listed here (redundant double-bake). zsh +
# zsh-completions + zoxide are small, universal, OFFICIAL-repo packages → baked
# so `iictl shell set zsh` (the flagship switch) is fully OFFLINE. The heavier /
# AUR-only extras (nushell theming helpers, fizsh, carapace, oh-my-posh) are
# fetched online on demand via packages/optional/shells.list — never baked.
zsh
zsh-completions
zoxide
btop
eza
bat
ripgrep
ripgrep-all
repgrep
fd
fzf
skim
zellij
7zip
lazygit

# Desktop
zed
vlc
kdeconnect
strawberry

# Fallback/stability kernel — `linux` is always present as the primary
linux-lts
linux-lts-headers

# Office & creative
onlyoffice-bin
inkscape
gimp
obs-studio

# Dev
base-devel
git
neovim
code
rustup
uv
docker
docker-compose
podman
claude-code

# Dev baseline (small, universal — see PROPOSAL §7)
# NOT here: jq, yq, ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd — they already arrive as upstream
# PKGBUILD depends (jq + go-yq from illogical-impulse-basic, the Nerd Font from
# illogical-impulse-fonts-themes), so baking them is a redundant double-bake.
github-cli
git-delta
direnv
just
mise
distrobox

# Fonts — broaden emoji glyph coverage beyond upstream's ttf-twemoji
noto-fonts-emoji

# Printing / scanning / bluetooth (bluetooth.service is already enabled by
# ii-post-install; bluez-utils just adds the codecs + CLI). cups is socket-
# activated, so ii-post-install links cups.socket into sockets.target.wants.
cups
cups-pdf
bluez-utils
sane
simple-scan

# System
snapper
snap-pac
flatpak

# Theme coherence (#26 / PROPOSAL §9) — fill the non-color gaps upstream's
# matugen pipeline leaves open. matugen owns the COLOR css (gtk-3.0/gtk.css);
# these set the orthogonal widget-theme / icon / cursor NAMES via the unowned
# gtk-3.0/settings.ini + ~/.icons/default seams (overlay/skel-distro). Small +
# universal: adw-gtk3 is the canonical Adwaita-shaped GTK theme, Papirus the
# stock icon set, Bibata (AUR — auto-routed to prebuild by 40-packages.sh) the
# cursor. NOT plymouth — that is opt-in only (iictl theme plymouth), never baked.
adw-gtk3
papirus-icon-theme
bibata-cursor-theme
